# Is it a dinosaur?
subtitle: "T. rex, a pterodactyl, a chicken, a mammoth: tap every true dinosaur, and find out why one of them lays your breakfast eggs."

## Is it a dinosaur?
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: nhm
      title: Are birds dinosaurs? / What is a dinosaur?
      authors: Natural History Museum, London
      year: 2023
      finding: birds are living theropod dinosaurs; pterosaurs, plesiosaurs and Dimetrodon are not dinosaurs
    - id: birds
      title: IOC World Bird List
      authors: F. Gill, D. Donsker, P. Rasmussen (eds)
      year: 2024
      finding: about 11,000 living bird species

    card title "Is it a dinosaur?"

Seven famous animals, and one from the farmyard. Only some of them are dinosaurs.
    cards zoo cites ["nhm"] y 640 select Dinosaurs
        * "T. rex" icon.of t-rex icon.set twemoji in true
        * "Pterodactyl" in false
        * "Chicken" icon.of chicken icon.set twemoji in true
        * "Mammoth" icon.of mammoth icon.set twemoji in false
        * "Triceratops" in true
        * "Plesiosaur" in false
        * "Dimetrodon" in false
        * "Stegosaurus" in true

    ask "Which of these animals are dinosaurs? Tap every dinosaur, then Done." on zoo store d feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "A palaeontologist in disguise." feedback.good "The museum would hire you." feedback.poor "Even museums mixed these up for years." feedback.none "The chicken fooled you, didn't it?"
        right: All {d.total} right.
        wrong: {d} of {d.total} on the first try.

Tyrannosaurus, Triceratops and Stegosaurus are the easy ones.
    highlight zoo_1 zoo_5 zoo_8

    text g_ptero "Pterodactyl: flying reptile" #b5482e x 500 y 240 font_size 40

But the pterodactyl is not a dinosaur. Pterosaurs were flying reptiles, cousins on a branch of their own.
    highlight zoo_2

    erase g_ptero

    text g_ples "Plesiosaur: sea reptile" #b5482e x 500 y 240 font_size 40

Plesiosaurs swam the seas, another branch of reptiles, and no dinosaurs either.
    highlight zoo_6

    erase g_ples

    text g_dime "Dimetrodon: kin of mammals" #b5482e x 500 y 240 font_size 40

And Dimetrodon, with the sail on its back, lived before the first dinosaurs, and is closer kin to us mammals.
    highlight zoo_7

    erase g_dime

    text g_mam "Mammoth: a mammal" #b5482e x 500 y 240 font_size 40

The mammoth is plainly a mammal: an elephant in a woolly coat.
    highlight zoo_4

    erase g_mam

Which leaves the surprise: the chicken.
    highlight zoo_3

    text g_chick "Chicken: a living dinosaur" #2f6b8f cites ["birds"] x 500 y 240 font_size 40

Birds descend from the same group of meat-eating dinosaurs as Tyrannosaurus, so biologists count them as dinosaurs.
    highlight zoo_3

So the dinosaurs never all died out: about eleven thousand species of them are still flying around us.
    highlight zoo_3 effect circle
---
